id: pm-gh1671
title: "GH-1671: linked tests have no setup step, so every command embeds its build and --add re-runs heavy suites just to fix metadata"
description: "GitHub issue #1671 (reported 2026-11-05 against 2026.11.4 from three fleet PR reviews: pm-vcs#182, pm-rl#145 and pm-linear#208). Linked test commands have no setup or prerequisite step. In TypeScript extension packages the specs import built output (../dist/index.js), so a linked command works only after npm run build, and every command must embed npm run build && itself (5 linked commands on pm-rl, each rebuilding). CodeRabbit flagged the missing build on all three PRs. Because pm test <id> --add verifies by running the command, a metadata-only fix re-runs every heavy suite (300-750 s each on pm-rl). Expected: a declared per-item or per-tracker setup step (for example pm test <id> --setup \"npm run build\" or a tests.setup settings key) that pm test --run executes once before the linked commands, recorded with provenance like the commands, cached by input digest where possible, and reported as a typed setup_failed result distinct from test failures. Also an explicit way to add a command without running it, recorded as verified false in provenance, so metadata fixes need no re-run. Why it matters for agents: linked tests are the evidence the next agent reproduces with pm test --run; a missing build today fails with a confusing module-not-found error, and the only workaround multiplies run time. Duplicate check: searched linked test setup, prerequisite, build step and pm test --run across all statuses. pm-dlvv (closed) added per-linked-test env directives, and pm-mf5z, pm-44iu and pm-wn34 (closed) enforce runnable command-required linked tests; none adds a setup phase or unverified add."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,extensions,"gh:1671",linked-tests,sdk
created_at: "2026-11-05T20:48:02.161Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-13T22:54:51.260Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-13T21:04:48.138Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-13T21:04:48.138Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "A per-item or per-tracker setup command can be declared through CLI, SDK and MCP, is stored with provenance, and pm test --run executes it once before the linked commands; A failing setup step is reported as a typed setup_failed result distinct from test failures, and no linked command runs after it; An explicit add-without-run option records the command with verified false in provenance, and pm test --run still executes it; Negative control: removing the setup execution makes a spec whose linked command needs the setup output fail"
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: medium
severity: medium
repro_steps: "In a TypeScript extension package whose specs import ../dist/index.js: pm test <id> --add command='node --test test/x.test.js' on a clean checkout fails with module-not-found until the command embeds npm run build &&, and each --add re-runs the suite"
resolution: "New src/sdk/test/run-phases.ts: phase grammar (setup|test, test stored as absent), withLinkedTestSetupEntries (setups prepended to any selection naming a regular command; selected_indexes in run order; setup_indexes for unnamed setups), orderLinkedTestsSetupFirst for test-all, createLinkedTestSetupGate (setup rows marked phase: setup; executed failure -> setup_failed with setup_failure_cause; refusals keep their category; every later entry skipped without executing; setups exempt from empty-run and PM-assertion requirements) and the failure-category counters with setup_failed. phase is accepted by --add, --add-json, pm create/update --test and --set-json, kept by normalizeLinkedTest, excluded from identity and trust fingerprint, never deduplicated across test-all items, and never satisfies --measure. requiredItemFormatVersion returns 3 for a setup entry and CURRENT_ITEM_FORMAT_VERSION is 3; create now stamps the required format. --add/--add-json help reads 'Link isolated test; runs only with --run' (add never executed). Published-artifact matrix asserts 2026.10.9/10.10/10.13 refuse a format-3 setup item byte-identically. Follow-ups: pm-i0oazv (reuse passed setup in source-mode test-all), pm-04mzfl (write-time warning for pins that cannot read format 3)."
expected_result: A declared setup step runs once per pm test --run before linked commands with provenance and a typed setup_failed result; an add records a command without running it
actual_result: "Verified: tests/integration/linked-tests/linked-test-setup-phase.integration.spec.ts (negative control fails without the setup; setup_failed skips later entries and the CLI exits non-zero; test-all runs each item's setup; every intake path accepts phase and refuses unknown phases before persistence), tests/unit/sdk/test/run-phases.spec.ts (7 cases), workspace-compatibility matrix passed against real published hosts, and the published 2026.11.13 refuses get/update/test --run on a format-3 item without changing bytes"
affected_version: 2026.11.4
component: test
